            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite5/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/yosemite5-phosphor-multi-gpio-monitor.json",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "What happens when the line changes before the BMC boots up? Do you want to use the INIT_HIGH and INIT_LOW Targets as well so you can do the necessary line level changes of the output based on the init-value of the input?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-yosemite5/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/yosemite5-phosphor-multi-gpio-monitor.json",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "KenChen",
                        "email": "Ken.Chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "jungle0220"
                    },
                    "message": "hi @amithash@meta.com\n\nYes, init RST_PCIE_E1S_0_PERST/RST_PCIE_E1S_1_PERST based on the value of RST_PCIE_BOOT_PERST_N.\n\nRST_PCIE_BOOT_PERST_N is low when HOST OFF.\nRST_PCIE_BOOT_PERST_N changes from lower to high when HOST POWER ON initially reaches a certain stage.\nRST_PCIE_BOOT_PERST_N Strong timing requirements. so EE change this gpio signal bypass by HW."
                }
            ],
